cd /home/axel/LeanAlgebraicGeometry-Horizon && "$HORIZON_BIN" inbox add --kind info --to horizon --body "RELEASE ajcr-p3: AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-d.ddr.divrep.abel-widened -- LANDED (not a gate closure). Owner cleared, pinned 850624c64c. What not to re-derive, and one pricing of mine that is REFUTED.

DO NOT REDO -- Picard/DivisorFamilyAffAbel.lean, rooted at AlgebraicJacobian.lean:627. 10 declarations, sorry-free, ALL axiom-clean [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] against a control that fired sorryAx; lake build EXIT=0 (8958 jobs). Census, non-vacuity, and hdegAff's load-bearing status independently CONFIRMED by fresh-context audit (I-1098/I-1099/I-1100). Commits eb72ffe94c / 9f57a2b326 / 93259ae1ae; the middle content also rode c2e6be0573 (another lane's sweep).
 * abelDivAffPlus, abelDivAffPlus_mapAlgHom -- unit . relPicMk . DivFamZarAff.picClass and its naturality in the test algebra;
 * abelDivAffPlus_toAff -- agreement with the chart-typed hook, so this EXTENDS the Abel layer along divFunctorToAff rather than forking it (NOT rfl: plain rfl fails on a type mismatch);
 * abelDivAff', abelDivAff'_val, picEtMap_abelDivAff' -- the widened Abel value at an arbitrary test and its naturality;
 * chartValueAff, picEtMap_chartValueAff, chartValueAff_mem_pic0Subgroup -- the degree-zero twist, which is FREE (sigmaFamily/thetaFamily are Cech classes on the base-changed curve and never saw a divisor cover);
 * degAt_abelDivAff'_toAff -- hdegAff's inhabitation witness.
8 of the 10 are pi-FREE.

THE GAP THIS FILLED. DivFamZarAff (mandated by I-0492) had picClass and its naturalities, divFunctorAff, and divFunctorToAff -- and ZERO declarations reaching PicEtAff/picEt/relPic/pic0. The whole Abel layer sat at chart-typed DivFamZar. So the two DD-R halves pointed at different functors: abelSigmaChart (Pic0AtlasFromDivRep.lean:205) consumes a representation of the CHART-TYPED divFunctor, while isCertified_affine_and_not_isCertified_chart puts a straddling divisor on the widened side out of chart-typed reach.

MY PRICING, REFUTED -- do not inherit it. I wrote that the widened degree ledger is OBSTRUCTED because deg_presentationDivisor_eq_finrank_glued cites relCover_sup with cover0/cover1. FALSE (I-1098; I re-derived it before accepting). Those lines OUTPUT only 'every point lies in some piece', which the widened side carries as the structure FIELD AffCoverData.cover, extracted as exists_mem_pieces (DivisorFamilyAffCover.lean:166). The pinned pair was the chart-typed COST of a fact AffCoverData ASSUMES. DO NOT open a 'recover the pinned pair' front.

THE HONEST RESIDUE: port four lemmas -- finrank_glued_eq_sum_of_separated (:144), subsingleton_ovlColength_of_sep (:308), finrank_colength_eq_sum (:217), coeffAt_eq_zero_of_isUnit_germ (:282), all DivisorFamilyFieldDegree.lean -- each quantifying ONLY over A.index/A.pieces/A.eqn/A.colength/A.ovlColength/A.Glued, all carried verbatim by AffAdaptation, none mentioning m0/m1/h0/h1/partitions or a chart. Real work, NOT blocked. That drops hdegAff, which is the whole remaining distance to a widened chartValueTrans (divFunctorAff => pic0TypeFunctor) and hence to a widened Sigma-chart.

ALSO CORRECTED, since three of my notes said it: rep is NOT an antecedent of pic0RepresentableByOfCharts. That declaration takes f, hf and the IsLocallySurjective instance. rep is an argument of abelSigmaChart and mixedParamRepresentableBy (Pic0ChartAtlasParamFree.lean:127) -- upstream of the assembly, not inside it. rep remains UNDISCHARGED and no gate cleared." 2>&1 | tail -3

